  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can Bridges Industrial build a custom website for my business?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Bridges Industrial designs and develops modern, responsive websites tailored to your brand, workflow, and operational needs. We handle everything from domain setup through hosting and maintenance, and hosting comes with the portal and dashboards to work in."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you integrate payment systems, online stores, or POS platforms?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. We build custom eCommerce systems, online storefronts, and point-of-sale integrations that connect seamlessly with your inventory, CRM, and financial tools."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you connect my systems, replace expensive software, or build dashboards for my data?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, and it is one capability rather than three products. We write the logic that connects your instruments, systems, and data sources, then serve it securely. Take the API into your own system, or have us host it with a front end to work in. Hosting comes with the API, so it is the same connection either way. Connecting into an existing control or historian system is scoped per project rather than sold off the shelf."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does Bridges Industrial offer industrial hardware for field data collection?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. PragOptics, our hardware and software group, builds the Omni product line of published field hardware. You can buy it assembled, or build one for yourself from the published schematic, BOM, and print-ready case files at pragoptics.com. Personal and in-house builds are permitted; manufacturing for resale is not. OmniSource, a pocket loop-power supply, is released. OmniPulse is a HART communicator in development, arriving ahead of OmniBus, and is OmniBus without loop power or milliamp measurement. OmniBus is a vendor-agnostic HART communicator and calibration recorder expected Q4 2027, carrying loop power and milliamp measurement, Bluetooth, iOS app integration, standalone field operation, calibration datalogging over HTTPS, a local WiFi hotspot, and GPS location tracking."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you provide industrial automation or instrumentation support?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Field instrumentation and analytical measurement are the core of what we do: calibration, configuration, commissioning, loop verification, smart device support, and diagnostics for intermittent faults and hard-to-measure products, across all major instrument OEMs. We also read, change, and troubleshoot the control logic running on PLC and DCS platforms."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can Bridges Industrial design and build custom hardware for a project?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. PragOptics designs and builds custom field-data devices, control boards, and enclosures, from a one-off proof of concept through a short production batch. That covers schematic capture, PCB layout, board bring-up, firmware and embedded logic, enclosure design, and assembly. The Omni product line is the open-hardware example of that work."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you offer 3D printing or short-run production parts?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. We run MSLA (masked stereolithography) printing in photopolymer resin, which suits parts needing fine feature detail and a smooth surface finish: prototypes and proof-of-concept parts, custom enclosures and housings, jigs and fixtures, replacement or discontinued components, and short batch production runs."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you write custom control logic for a machine or process?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. We develop function and control logic for custom projects, whether commissioning something new or replacing logic on equipment already in service. That covers PLC and DCS logic across major OEM platforms, motor, relay and interlock logic, PID tuning and control strategy, safety instrumented functions, and custom sequence logic for one-off machines."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I use PragOptics software to build things myself?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "That is the goal. The PragOptics platform, now in development, puts our own workflow in customers' hands: design your own hardware, write and test your own function logic against real hardware, build and publish web apps, and clean up and visualize your data. Your own Field Node Manager, running your logic instead of ours. It runs in the browser, with a cloud option that provisions environments and storage once an account is active."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you fix an intermittent or unexplained measurement problem?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Readings that drift, wander, or fail only intermittently, and products that are genuinely hard to measure, are some of our most requested work. Most are not instrument failures but a process meeting an instrument that was never matched to it: product flashing across an orifice, low-density solids that radar sees through, coating, foam, entrained gas, or stratification. We determine whether the device already installed can be made reliable through mounting, ranging, or configuration, or whether the technology genuinely cannot see the product, and explain the reasoning either way."
      }
    }
  ]
}

